WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
So, let's talk about pricing and usage

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.870
for a moment because this is actually

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.710
quite an important topic, especially as

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.590
you use Claude Code more and more and

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.350
you eventually run into rate limits. To

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.270
give a quick overview, Anthropic

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.710
basically has a free plan where you can

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.110
use the Claude chat app. So, this does

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.990
not include Claude Code. This only

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.310
includes the ChatGPT equivalent of

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.670
Anthropic, which is claude.ai. Now, to

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.550
use Claude Code, as we know, you need to

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.270
have the Pro plan. So, this is $17 USD

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.710
if you are on the annual subscription,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.230
but for most people who are on the

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.710
monthly, this is $20. And this Pro plan

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.990
is the minimum that you need in order to

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.750
access Claude Code. And obviously, for

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.950
most people, I would advise you to start

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.590
with this plan as well. Now, the highest

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.110
tier for Anthropic is their Max plan.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.990
And there's actually sort of two

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.510
sub-tiers from within Max because if you

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.190
look at the sub-note here, it says that

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.150
it has everything in Pro, so all of the

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.150
benefits in here, but you can choose

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.310
either 5x or 20x more usage. And if you

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.670
look at Claude's documentation here, you

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.030
can see a bit more detail in this table,

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.990
where essentially the price of the Max

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.710
5x plan is $100 per month, where the 20x

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.470
plan is $200 per month. Now, when we say

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.230
5x or 20x, that just means that you have

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.110
5x the token budgets of the Pro plan,

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.110
while this one has 20x the token budgets

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.630
of the Pro plan. But that begs the

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.390
question, what is a token anyway? And

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.590
it's actually simpler than you think.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.190
Whenever you talk to a chatbot or an AI

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.950
agent similar to Claude Code or even

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.550
ChatGPT, when you send a prompt, that is

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.750
broken down into what we're calling as

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.310
tokens. And when ChatGPT or Claude

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.110
thinks about the result of that prompt

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.070
and sends a result back to you, what it

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.910
does is generate text, a lot of text,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.150
that can be converted into tokens. Now,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.350
for simplicity's sake, a token you can

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.910
think of as basically four letters. So,

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.510
let's say you have the sentence called

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.190
"Build your operating system." This

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.470
consists of five tokens in total. So,

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.990
whenever you see tokens being talked

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.790
about in the AI world, or you see your

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.310
AI agents counting the amount of tokens

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.310
that it is consuming, that's all just

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.150
clusters of four to five-letter words,

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.870
depending on the letter. And so, you can

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.750
think of tokens as the basic unit of

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.670
working with these AI agents, and a

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.310
basic unit of AI in general. Similar to

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.710
now that we're using the internet, what

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.750
is the basic unit? It's kilobytes,

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.270
megabytes, gigabytes, right? It's the

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.710
amount of data that is coursing through

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.190
the network. In fact, this analogy is

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.790
actually pretty good, because if you

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.949
think about buying internet now, you can

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:31.110
subscribe to a mobile data plan, and

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.910
it's similar in a sense that you can

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.110
subscribe for, let's say, $60 a month,

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.670
and you get a set amount of budget for

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.510
the data that you have. So, to give an

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.670
example, here in Optus in Australia, you

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.910
can think of this as sort of your max

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.430
plan, and maybe this one would be your

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.190
pro or standard plan. Now, the big

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.230
difference between these AI labs, at

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:51.590
least at the moment, is that

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.790
unfortunately, unlike Telco providers

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.790
and data plan providers, where you

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.830
literally see the absolute value of

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.350
gigabytes that you get for each plan,

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.390
right now, the way that Anthropic and

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.229
OpenAI, and even Google are displaying

00:03:05.239 --> 00:03:07.430
these token budgets to you on these

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.830
different subscription tiers, is not in

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.830
absolute. So, you can see that these

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.550
higher tiers only say that it is five

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.070
times the amount of pro, and this one is

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.030
20 times the amount of pro, but they

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.470
don't actually publish how many million

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.870
tokens this is in total. Hopefully, that

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.110
will change, but right now, that is our

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.070
reality. And so, this becomes important,

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.670
because if you go to Claude Code, and

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.830
you want to check your usage or your

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.910
token budgets that are remaining, if you

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.590
type in {slash} usage, what that will do

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.270
is just allow you to see what your

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.150
remaining usage is. And at least for

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.150
Claude Code, right now, there are three

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.830
limits to take note of. One is a limit

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.390
per session. So, let's say for me, I

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.070
started this session 2 hours ago, and

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.110
you can see it resets in 3 hours, so

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.950
it's a whole 5 hour session. And I still

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.430
have around 89% of my token budget

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.550
remaining. Now, for the whole week, it

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.150
just reset earlier, and so this whole

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.750
thing would reset in 6 days. And because

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:06.030
it just reset, then now I have a fresh

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.790
token budget of a remaining 98% for

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.190
today up until 6 days from now. Now,

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.550
you're using Sonnet as a default, then

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.830
this weekly Sonnet usage limit will also

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.590
be relevant to you. But that's basically

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.750
a weekly allocation of tokens that you

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.910
can just use the Sonnet model for.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.590
Recently, Anthropic also included some

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.270
default insights here on what's

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.350
contributing to your limits usage. So,

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.190
you can just go and filter that by day

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.030
or by week, and you'll be able to

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.590
understand where your usage is going if

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.270
in case you're trying to manage this

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.760
better.
